WEBVTT

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:13.450
While racing in the dark,
Appare and Kosame appeared in front of me.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:16.620
You guys are going to win
the Trans-America Wild Race?!

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.330
That would be impossible!

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.660
Still, Appare touched on a dream of mine
that had nearly vanished.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.450
Be careful, you two.
This world is not a gentle one!

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:48.790
Who the hell are you?!

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:55.370
There, that's a good boy. Don't waste booze.

00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:56.700
H-How did you...?!

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:00.500
Oh, don't pull out your gun
if you don't want to die.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.370
Hey, let him go! You trying to
get yourself killed?!

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:06.000
Stop! This guy--I mean, this man...

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.540
...is Dylan, of the Thousand Three!

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:10.160
Thousand Three?!

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:12.910
Do not call me that.

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.000
Much obliged. You saved me.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:22.950
Get on out of here. This is no place
to be bringing a little kid.

00:02:22.950 --> 00:02:25.410
Huh? No, this isn't my child--

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:30.200
Wait. Have you seen a man
with this tattoo on his neck?

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:34.290
What are you going to do when you find him?

00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:37.200
I'm gonna take back what was stolen from us.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:40.870
Forget it. You'll get killed.

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:41.790
Wait!

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:43.580
Do you know something about him?!

00:02:45.250 --> 00:02:46.370
Hey,

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:49.580
you're the guy that was driving
that awesome car, right?

00:02:49.580 --> 00:02:51.450
You want an autograph?

00:02:51.450 --> 00:02:53.200
Don't forget this--

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:56.830
Someday, my car will be
driving in front of yours.

00:02:56.830 --> 00:03:00.950
Hey, don't be rude to him! He saved us!

00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:06.200
--Hmph, do as you will.
--Huh?

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:10.370
I didn't save you; I just want to
enjoy some good booze.

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:18.950
Ah, hey! Are you okay?!

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:30.870
Dad...!

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:32.950
Get out of here, Hototo!

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.500
Dad!

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:57.660
You should eat that.

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:03.700
Where is this?

00:04:03.700 --> 00:04:07.500
A storehouse at the harbor. We live here.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:11.910
What are you doing?

00:04:11.910 --> 00:04:14.870
Rebuilding a ship into a car
and entering a race.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:17.700
Huh? Turning a boat into a car?

00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:23.080
Oh, you're awake?

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:27.870
Ah, I told you, stop using my
sword stand as your trash can!

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:34.080
I'm Kosame. That's Appare.
Are you okay, little boy?

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.830
Where's your family? Are you alone?

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:39.000
I'm not a little boy.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:44.450
My name is Hototo. My family is far away.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:47.620
My mother, my sister, and my brothers.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:52.290
I came here alone, from far to the east,
and far to the north,

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:55.370
to take back what was stolen from us.

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:57.410
What was stolen from you?

00:04:57.410 --> 00:05:01.410
Our land, our home, our horses...

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:04.500
...and my father's life.

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:08.200
I don't know what you've been through,

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:11.870
but once you're healed up,
you should go back to your family.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:16.120
What can a child like you do against
someone who took your father's life?

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:19.790
Don't treat me like a child,
when you're so weak.

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.660
I won't forget your kindness
in offering me this food and water.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:26.120
But I do not follow the words of a weakling.

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:30.790
Hey, where do you mean,
far to the east and far to the north?

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:37.410
Around here, I think.
It was farther to the east long ago.

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:39.330
Until our land was taken.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.040
Tell me something, what's the elevation
of these mountains?

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.410
--I need to know a route to cross them in a car.

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:44.450
--Well, um...
--I need to know a route to cross them in a car.

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:46.160
How steep and broad is the incline?

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:48.790
Are there places along the way
where we can resupply?

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:49.870
Also, what about the weather and temperature--

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:50.950
Appare!

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:54.250
Enough, let him rest.
You'll aggravate his injuries.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:55.410
Yeah, okay.

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:05.200
"Episode 3"
"Duel"

00:06:19.660 --> 00:06:21.790
There isn't much rain in this area.

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:24.120
--It could be hard to obtain water
anywhere but this river.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:25.160
--Get out?!
--It could be hard to obtain water
anywhere but this river.

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:27.000
Yeah, I'm sorry.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.500
But it's so heartless!

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:34.160
What can I do? Someone came along
who wants to rent all the storehouses.

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:37.580
He's some rich lad who came here from Europe.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:40.450
He said he didn't care what it would cost.

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:43.700
They're unloading his stuff
from that huge ship over there.

00:06:46.790 --> 00:06:48.700
Hey, where are you going?

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:49.580
To tell him no.

00:06:49.580 --> 00:06:51.580
Huh? Tell him no? What are you talking about?!

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:55.250
N-Nice! Way to go, Appare! I'm coming, too!

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:03.450
Take this to my tent. I'd like to
check on what's inside right away.

00:07:03.450 --> 00:07:08.250
Al, how about some tea? I'm sure everyone
is worn out from the long trip.

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:11.910
You're right, Sofia. Thanks.

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:15.870
You sure are fired up.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:18.540
Of course. I'm going to win this race,

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:24.500
and show everyone that I'm
talented enough to take over BNW.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:28.830
You don't have to do all that.
Everyone recognizes how strong you are.

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:30.910
No, not yet they don't.

00:07:30.910 --> 00:07:35.950
Automobiles are still only a fledgling part
of our family's businesses.

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:41.040
But Dad and my brothers won't even let me,
the youngest, take that over.

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:46.620
I'm going to win this race, convince Dad,
and put my brothers in their place.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:50.620
Pardon!

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:52.950
There you are.

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.040
Oh, thank you.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:58.830
So you're saying you want to
keep using the storehouse as before?

00:07:58.830 --> 00:07:59.910
Yeah.

00:07:59.910 --> 00:08:03.620
Aren't the other storehouses enough
to house the belongings from your ship?

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:08.370
That is none of your business.
I will use as many storehouses as I need.

00:08:08.370 --> 00:08:10.200
So get out, right now.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:11.370
Al...

00:08:12.290 --> 00:08:15.910
I'm not just housing my things.
I'm tuning and testing my machine;

00:08:15.910 --> 00:08:18.660
I also need a break area for my staff,
a training space for me,

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:20.750
and a dog run for Alfred.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:23.660
I'm short on space as it is.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:25.250
Your machine?

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:26.500
That over there.

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:31.370
The cream of BNW's technology
all gathered into--

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:34.580
He seems surprised.

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:38.540
Um, isn't there something you can do?
At least leave us a place to sleep.

00:08:38.540 --> 00:08:41.540
If you have nowhere to sleep,
you can go to a hotel.

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:47.370
We're going to make full use of this place
until the Trans-America Wild Race.

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:49.910
You all are entering the race, too?

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:55.790
Yes. I'm Al Lyon. I'm entering the race
on behalf of BNW,

00:08:55.790 --> 00:08:59.370
one of the Big Three automotive association
B.I.G.BOSS's members,

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:01.330
and I'm going to win.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:02.830
So we're rivals, then.

00:09:02.830 --> 00:09:06.200
Huh? You guys are entering the race, too?

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:07.040
Yeah.

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:10.330
Ah! Laymen shouldn't be touching that!

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:13.700
Incredible. This is much more
elegant and well-honed

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:15.660
than any other car I've seen before.

00:09:15.660 --> 00:09:19.950
Of course it is. There's no
better car in all the world.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:23.250
But the basic design is
exactly like the other cars.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:27.160
Also, it's <i>too </i>elegant.
There's room for improvement here.

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:29.040
What do you even know?

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.910
I know. Why don't you race my car?

00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:34.040
Huh? <i>Your </i>car?

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:38.080
If I win, we get to use
the storehouse as we like.

00:09:39.910 --> 00:09:43.290
Give me ten days, and I'll turn that
into a car that yours can't beat.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:46.580
That's not a car, it's a broken-down boat!

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:48.000
Interesting. Let's do it.

00:09:48.000 --> 00:09:48.830
Huh?

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:52.120
We'll race in ten days. You're free
to choose the course, too.

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:56.540
If you win, I'll let you use
the storehouse as you like.

00:09:56.540 --> 00:09:59.250
On the other hand, what if I win?

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:01.160
<i>You </i>use the storehouse however <i>you </i>like.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:06.200
No, the storehouse is mine to begin with.
That wouldn't be a fair contest.

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:08.080
Then Kosame will commit hara-kiri.

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:09.040
Huh?

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.250
What?

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:15.370
I don't want to see him commit hara-kiri.
How about instead...

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:18.750
...I'll take your swords?

00:10:18.750 --> 00:10:20.290
Huh?!

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:28.790
My noble katanas have been in
the Isshiki family for generations.

00:10:28.790 --> 00:10:30.200
So we'll win.

00:10:30.200 --> 00:10:32.410
I've got it! What if we made
the course in the ocean?

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:33.410
No.

00:10:33.410 --> 00:10:35.080
Then we're sunk.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:39.870
You shouldn't be going out so much.
Your injuries haven't yet--

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:41.580
What are you doing with those?

00:10:41.580 --> 00:10:45.410
I can't keep living off of you guys,
when you're so poor.

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:46.660
Did you steal those?

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:52.410
I caught them. Nature will provide
everything you need, if you respect it.

00:10:52.410 --> 00:10:56.200
You guys have one, too.
I'll smoke whatever is left.

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:59.830
That is helpful, but you're just a child.

00:10:59.830 --> 00:11:01.330
You don't have to be so considerate toward us--

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:03.790
Okay, none for you, Kosame.

00:11:03.790 --> 00:11:06.200
Appare, do you want two?

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:08.830
There, finished.

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:11.120
What is that?

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:15.370
A windup-assisted two-wheeler.
I'm going out for a bit.

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:18.040
Hototo, I'd like my fish grilled.

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:19.080
Okay.

00:11:19.080 --> 00:11:20.620
Where are you going?

00:11:20.620 --> 00:11:25.040
I have to turn this into a car in ten days.
I'll need more parts.

00:11:26.750 --> 00:11:28.540
Oh, I'll come with you!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.580
Can you look after things here by yourself?

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:35.200
I was right; no food for you, Kosame.

00:11:37.620 --> 00:11:40.870
What? The trans-continental race?

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:42.330
Aren't we entering?

00:11:42.330 --> 00:11:45.830
Of course we aren't. If we compete
in that and wreck our car,

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:48.250
it will threaten the survival of our team.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:53.040
Besides, our cars aren't tough enough
to go across the country.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:54.540
I see.

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:57.750
Good going, David! Keep that up
in tomorrow's race...

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:03.450
Appare...?

00:12:07.910 --> 00:12:11.000
Are you sure we can take this stuff?

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:12.250
Yeah.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:17.250
This place is for parts from
wrecked cars that may still be useful.

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:19.410
But nobody oversees it,

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:23.080
and once they need the space,
they'll just be disposed of.

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:24.250
Thanks.

00:12:24.250 --> 00:12:27.450
That's okay. You helped me, too.

00:12:27.450 --> 00:12:31.290
Appare is the one who repaired it.
I just watched him.

00:12:31.290 --> 00:12:36.700
Kosame insisted I do it. I wanted
to soup it up even faster.

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:41.250
Have you driven at all since then?

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:44.160
--No.
--What a shame.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:47.160
This place is a gold mine.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:51.910
Are you serious about building a car
that can beat a BNW in ten days?

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:54.620
Yeah. It's a short-distance race.

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:57.750
A simple objective only
calls for a simple machine.

00:12:57.750 --> 00:12:59.830
I already have blueprints for it.

00:12:59.830 --> 00:13:02.540
What if you lose? The katanas are one thing,

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:04.870
but you'll have nowhere to live, right?

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:09.870
He is a self-centered fellow
with no manners, to be sure,

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:14.040
but he isn't a liar, and he doesn't
say what he can't back up.

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:15.700
Kosame, help me.

00:13:15.700 --> 00:13:17.250
Okay, okay.

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:21.330
I can't believe I doubted him for even a second.

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:24.160
Who's going to carry all of this back?

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:29.450
I'll be back if I need more.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:32.200
Come on, you're supposed to say
"thank you very much."

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:34.580
You can come and watch the race.

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:38.580
It's not possible. You'll never beat a BNW.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:42.250
That's what everyone thinks.
Which is what makes it so interesting.

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:45.750
Hmm? Hey, hold up...

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:54.080
Looks like your injuries are just about healed.

00:13:54.080 --> 00:13:56.950
Children sure recover quickly, all right.

00:13:56.950 --> 00:14:01.330
The weaker you are, the more you
look down on others. Grandpa was right.

00:14:01.330 --> 00:14:07.870
I'm not looking down on you. Whatever you
might think, children are children--

00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:09.910
Hey, watch it!

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:15.580
You seem to be enjoying yourselves.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:17.120
Mr. Lyon...

00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:20.290
Call me Al. Who's he? Your boy?

00:14:20.290 --> 00:14:23.200
--No!
--No. This is Hototo.

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:25.410
It's a long story, but we're
stuck together right now.

00:14:27.120 --> 00:14:31.540
Nice to meet you, Hototo. How are you?

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:32.830
Fine.

00:14:32.830 --> 00:14:35.290
This is Sofia. She's my...

00:14:35.290 --> 00:14:39.500
I am Al's chaperone, to make sure
he doesn't do anything crazy.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:41.750
I was sure you were his older sister.

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:45.410
My mother is a domestic,
and served as Al's babysitter, so...

00:14:45.410 --> 00:14:49.290
Sofia, let's go. We can tour around
Los Angeles as we warm up the...

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:55.750
I'm going to go find us a course.
Hototo, come with me.

00:14:55.750 --> 00:14:57.250
--Okay.
--What is that?!

00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:59.580
A windup-assisted two-wheeler.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:01.450
Can I ride it for a minute?

00:15:01.450 --> 00:15:03.120
No.

00:15:03.120 --> 00:15:06.370
Don't be so stingy. You can
at least let him try it, right?

00:15:06.370 --> 00:15:08.830
Yeah, he's right--

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:12.330
Okay, if you win our race, I'll give it to you.

00:15:12.330 --> 00:15:13.870
Do you mean it?! Yes!

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:17.160
But in return, if I win, I'll take your car.

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:18.950
That's awfully bold.

00:15:18.950 --> 00:15:22.540
Hey, I know! Forget about my katanas,
and we'll trade for the storehouse--

00:15:22.540 --> 00:15:23.370
You got it.

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:24.660
Huh?

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:28.450
I am 100% going to win this.

00:15:28.450 --> 00:15:29.910
Al...

00:15:29.910 --> 00:15:32.450
We have an agreement. Don't forget.

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:45.870
They aren't coming.

00:15:45.870 --> 00:15:50.910
Yeah. I'm sure he must have backed out.
There's no way he could... beat me.

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:53.830
Huh...?

00:16:01.200 --> 00:16:04.080
Go faster. We're late.

00:16:04.080 --> 00:16:06.700
In the sword world, whoever shows up last wins!

00:16:06.700 --> 00:16:08.620
Hototo is beating us. Trade places.

00:16:08.620 --> 00:16:12.500
No way! Have you forgotten yesterday's
test drive?! I'm not ready to die!

00:16:12.500 --> 00:16:15.540
You're exaggerating. And I put a seatbelt in.

00:16:18.250 --> 00:16:19.870
Sorry to keep you.

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:22.160
Rather than blame you for being late,

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:27.080
I should compliment you for making it
all the way here in that thing.

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:30.870
I'll be taking that. That, <i>and </i>your swords.

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:32.540
I'm prepared for the worst.

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:33.830
A warrior never goes back on his word.

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:36.080
--<i>You </i>don't get to say that!
--Huh?

00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:38.700
Do you want me to hold on to them
until the race is over?

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:41.540
Xialian...

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:42.910
You came?

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:45.870
Yeah. So you really built it.

00:16:45.870 --> 00:16:48.330
Yeah. And I'm gonna win.

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:54.290
I'm honestly surprised. But there's no way
this will be a race with that car.

00:16:54.290 --> 00:16:57.000
It really isn't possible.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:58.580
She's right.

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:01.580
You people are birds who cannot fly.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:05.000
Okay, let's get started.
It'll be a waste of time, though.

00:17:05.870 --> 00:17:08.910
Appare, on second thought, you drive.

00:17:08.910 --> 00:17:11.620
Yeah. I was always planning to.

00:17:13.910 --> 00:17:15.790
The starting line is here.

00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:18.830
We pass through the gap between
those rocks three km ahead, come back here,

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:22.000
and whoever touches
this tree first is the winner.

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:25.700
There's no road.
The entire wasteland is our track.

00:17:25.700 --> 00:17:27.870
Just the way I wanted.

00:17:27.870 --> 00:17:29.080
Are you good to go?

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:30.620
--Yeah.
--Yeah.

00:17:30.620 --> 00:17:32.290
Ready...

00:17:32.290 --> 00:17:33.370
--Go!
--Go!

00:17:36.790 --> 00:17:38.200
I'm not holding back!

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:41.370
It's the least I can do to be polite!

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:44.160
He's fast! So that's a BNW...

00:17:45.950 --> 00:17:47.290
Hurry, Appare!

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:50.500
Stop talking, or you'll
bite your tongue, Kosame.

00:17:53.370 --> 00:17:57.410
This is it! Here we go!

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:02.120
Appare is the sort whose personality changes
when he takes the wheel.

00:18:02.120 --> 00:18:04.330
Yeah!

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:07.160
No!

00:18:08.870 --> 00:18:10.290
Oh, this is good!

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:14.540
Sure enough, they're no match for his speed.

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:17.410
Appare knows that.

00:18:17.410 --> 00:18:20.250
Even so, he still intends to win.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:24.700
Appare, there's a cliff! Go around!

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:26.450
Hold on, Kosame!

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:27.540
Huh?

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:34.500
See for yourself if these birds can't fly!

00:18:34.500 --> 00:18:37.790
Wah! We're flying!

00:18:37.790 --> 00:18:40.370
We're dead!

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:41.950
You'll get through it!

00:18:47.700 --> 00:18:49.160
All right!

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:53.910
What a character! But there aren't
any other cliffs you can use for a shortcut.

00:18:53.910 --> 00:18:55.830
From here on, it's a contest of speed!

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:10.620
Damn it, it's no use.

00:19:10.620 --> 00:19:12.000
Kosame!

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:15.250
When I give the signal, pull the red lever
at your feet as hard as you can!

00:19:15.250 --> 00:19:17.580
Red lever? You mean this?

00:19:17.580 --> 00:19:21.330
We aren't going to lose.
The Appare will fly yet again.

00:19:21.330 --> 00:19:23.200
Huh? Again?

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:27.790
460 meters to the finish line... 40... 20...

00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:29.370
Now! Pull it!

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:39.370
Emergency acceleration booster, engage!

00:19:46.410 --> 00:19:50.160
Huh? H-Hey! H-Hold on...!

00:19:53.910 --> 00:19:55.040
--Oh...
--Oh...

00:20:03.620 --> 00:20:05.330
Oww...

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:09.040
I won't be beaten!

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:10.910
Kosame, run!

00:20:26.410 --> 00:20:27.910
They won...

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:31.790
Guess it was short after all.

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:34.120
After all? That was premeditated?!

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.410
Appare, I'm impressed.

00:20:35.410 --> 00:20:37.040
<i>I'm </i>the one who crossed the finish line!

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:38.410
Appare...

00:20:40.450 --> 00:20:42.830
You are completely nuts.

00:20:42.830 --> 00:20:45.750
There's no way you can make it
to the finish like that.

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:49.750
But you still won this one.

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:54.450
You came up with a strategy to let you win,

00:20:54.450 --> 00:20:57.250
chose the course, and built your car.

00:20:57.250 --> 00:21:01.620
I did nothing but be complacent and
rely on my car's performance, and I lost.

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:04.160
Are you sure about this?
What about the trans-continental race?

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:08.540
That is my spare second car.
I'm still entering the race, of course.

00:21:08.540 --> 00:21:11.120
My machine for the big race is even faster.

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:15.000
All right! We got a car!

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.620
Sofia, I'm sorry. We're walking back.

00:21:17.620 --> 00:21:18.870
Right.

00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:19.910
Al!

00:21:20.790 --> 00:21:23.910
I'm making a better car for the big race, too.

00:21:23.910 --> 00:21:27.620
Race me. Next time,
<i>I'll </i>be driving in front of <i>you</i>.

00:21:27.620 --> 00:21:31.450
Yeah, and <i>I'll </i>be the one
crossing the finish line first.

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:35.290
You can ride this back. It's yours.

00:21:36.250 --> 00:21:42.080
No, I lost. I can't very well
accept it. I'll walk back.

00:21:42.080 --> 00:21:43.910
Okay, <i>I'll </i>take it!

00:21:43.910 --> 00:21:45.120
--Huh?!
--Huh?!

00:21:50.290 --> 00:21:52.830
Ah, there, there, there, there...

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:53.950
See you.

00:21:53.950 --> 00:21:56.870
Uh, sure you don't want to
go back together in the car?

00:21:56.870 --> 00:21:57.950
Yeah.

00:22:01.410 --> 00:22:04.660
How far can I go?

00:22:11.080 --> 00:22:13.620
It's gonna take a little while to fix this.

00:22:13.620 --> 00:22:18.120
Appare, we <i>are </i>entering the big race
in the car we got from him, right?

00:22:18.120 --> 00:22:19.330
Huh?

00:23:28.910 --> 00:23:31.580
I'd like you to take care of this.

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:38.120
Let the world know that this is
not the beginning of a new age.

00:23:46.700 --> 00:23:47.450
"Next time"

00:23:47.450 --> 00:23:49.910
"Episode 4"
"Let It Go"
